es/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/logs/w9-T047.out:\n  Line 31: The line's steps alone do not satisfy its own verify. Without extra work the advisor in the arena exits `69` with `@spec-kit/system-skill-advisor dist is stale`, because `git clone` stamps every source with the checkout time while `cp -Rc` preserves the compiled build's older mtime, and the freshness guard's path-keyed cache record cannot survive a move to a new absolute path. I added one step after each copied `dist` tree: set its timestamps to the copy time, so the copied build (the same commit's build) looks newer than the checkout, as a build run there would. Evidence: before the step, `checkPackageFreshness` returned `status: \"stale\"` via the mtime branch; after it, `fresh` for both entries and the CLI returns a recommendation. The step touches only files inside the arena.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-speckit/memory-search-and-knowledge/003-memory-search-intelligence/scratch/topology-migration-backup/identity-backups/002-spec-data-quality/050-validate-sh-dist-freshness-and-repo-remediation/001-dist-freshness-enforcement/plan.md:\n  Line 63: - [x] OpenCode plugin warns (non-blocking) before a Bash call matching `opencode run` / `validate.sh` when a watched dist is stale; registers a `session.created` one-time summary.\n\n  Line 78: - **`check-dist-staleness.sh`** (new, sibling to `check-comment-hygiene.sh`): reads `tool_input.file_path` from the same stdin JSON payload `claude-posttooluse.sh` already parses; if the path falls under a watched source tree and dist is stale, prints the warning banner; always exits 0.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-speckit/memory-search-and-knowledge/003-memory-search-intelligence/scratch/topology-migration-backup/identity-backu